rem Dyalog Programming Contest 2011
rem Task 2: What's in a Name?
rem Noise: replace each letter of Name with X,
rem independently, with probability Rate.
rem Search: find every place Name occurs in Text
rem with at most Tolerance mismatched characters,
rem ignoring case. An empty Name or one longer
rem than Text has no matches.

use io
use cli
use random
use sequences
use text

rem Chance that each letter becomes X.
option Rate real = 0.2
rem Random seed, for repeatable noise.
option Seed integer = 42
rem Name to disturb and to look for.
option Name path = "Jack Johnson"
rem Text searched for the name.
option Text path = "I think Jakc Jonnson is the greatest"
rem Most mismatched characters allowed.
option Tolerance integer = 3

rem Spaces, digits and punctuation never
rem change; the number of changed letters is
rem random, not Rate times the letter count.
Seed seed
Chars = Name "" split
Shape = array (Chars len)
Draws = Shape 0 1 uniform
Mask = Draws less Rate and Chars letter
Letters = Mask choose "X" Chars
Noisy = Letters "" join
Noisy print

rem Hamming distance of every window of the
rem same width, compared in lowercase. The
rem original text is kept for the result.
Width = Name len
Positions = array shape 0 fill 0
Matches = array shape 0 fill ""
if Width at least 1
  Lower = (Text lower) "" split
  Windows = Lower window Width
  Pattern = (Name lower) "" split
  Different = Windows not equal Pattern
  Errors = Different count axis 1
  Close = Errors at most Tolerance
  Positions = Close indices
  Raw = Text window Width
  Matches = Raw Positions
end
Positions print
Matches print
